rows.24:5e38:
So I went around behind the old school building.
That day, too, the weather was fine. It was just right for sunbathing.
I poked just my head out from the shadow of the building and peeked at the spot where Takeuchi had been standing the other day.{p}

rows.24:7424:
Takeuchi was glaring at me with a terrifying face.
Can you believe it?
His body had turned greenish, his hands were covered in leaves, and from his feet, hundreds of root-like things had come out and stabbed into the ground.{p}

rows.24:78c8:
I squeezed my eyes shut, trying not to look at Takeuchi.
And then, you know, a breath that smelled like raw green grass blew softly across my face.
It was so gross I got goosebumps.{p}

